# index.lock is an append-only lockfile that every version PR appends to, so
# open PRs all conflict on it and serialize — only one can merge before the
# rest go stale. Resolve index.lock conflicts by keeping BOTH sides' additions
# (the built-in `union` merge driver) so version PRs stop blocking each other.
#
# This changes nothing about the file's format or content — every consumer
# (the AP-Pie web app's SHA verification, .github/scripts/detect_added_versions.py,
# the worker's open-pr.sh) keeps parsing it byte-identically. The only risk union
# introduces is two PRs adding the *same* "version" = "sha" line, which would be a
# duplicate key; the lint-toml workflow now parses index.lock with tomllib to catch
# exactly that.
index.lock merge=union
